title: Paradigm Platform spec written
summary: Wrote the comprehensive platform spec at docs/specs/platform.md (2,334 lines). Defines the vision for unifying all Paradigm tools (Lore, Graph, Sentinel, University, Symphony) into a single `paradigm serve` command and browser tab. 8 implementation phases from unified shell through methodology/certification. Introduces governance primitives (Vote, Promise, Deny), collaborative Graph with Context Panel, Git management UI, and structured meetings.
symbols_touched:
  - '#platform-server'
  - '#platform-ui'
  - $meeting-flow
symbols_created:
  - '#platform-server'
  - '#platform-ui'
  - $meeting-flow
files_created:
  - docs/specs/platform.md
lines_added: 2334
decisions:
  - id: D-platform-metaphor
    decision: Use 'The Studio' metaphor extending Symphony's live band
    rationale: Each tool is a channel on the mixing board, Graph is the live session room — natural extension of existing metaphor
  - id: D-platform-port
    decision: Default port 3850, coexist with standalone servers
    rationale: Don't break existing workflows — users can run both paradigm serve and paradigm lore serve
  - id: D-governance-primitives
    decision: 'Three governance primitives: Vote, Promise, Deny'
    rationale: Minimal but complete set — Vote for decisions, Promise for commitments, Deny for blocks. All create lore entries.
  - id: D-absorb-not-rewrite
    decision: Absorb existing UI components rather than rewriting
    rationale: Lore-ui and graph-ui work well. Copy into platform-ui sections, adapt API paths, delegate theme to shell.
  - id: D-sentinel-university-optional
    decision: Sentinel and University are auto-detected optional sections
    rationale: Not all users have these packages. Platform works without them. Auto-detect via import.
learnings:
  - Symphony spec format is 1692 lines with Vision, Architecture, CLI, Components, Phases, Security, Success Criteria — platform.md follows same structure at 2334 lines
  - Four existing UIs share React 18 + Zustand + Vite + CSS custom properties — consolidation is feasible
  - Sentinel has 31 UI components and 10 stores — re-export as components is preferred over iframe for same-React-version integration
